    {
      "id": "s11",
      "type": "TIMELINE",
      "transition": "morph",
      "background": "zoneA",
      "narration": "Because a plain assert checks once, instantly. You click Save. Assert looks for the toast at zero milliseconds, and the toast does not arrive until eight hundred. The check and the event sit at different places on the clock. Wrong verdict, flaky test.",
      "data": {
        "timeline": {
          "milestones": [
            {
              "date": "0 ms",
              "title": "you click Save",
              "color": "blue",
              "atWord": 6.25
            },
            {
              "date": "still 0 ms",
              "title": "assert: FAIL",
              "color": "red",
              "atWord": 8.917
            },
            {
              "date": "800 ms",
              "title": "toast arrives",
              "color": "orange",
              "atWord": 17.75
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "durationFrames": 476,
      "audio": "audio/pw-dojo-06-assertions_long_s11.mp3",
      "timingSource": "tts"
    },
    {
      "id": "s12",
      "type": "CYCLE_LOOP",
      "transition": "zoom",
      "background": "zoneB",
      "narration": "Expect is a patient critic. It checks, and if the answer is not true yet, it waits a moment and checks again, round and round, for up to five seconds. The instant that toast appears, it passes.",
      "data": {
        "cycleLoop": {
          "headline": "expect() re-checks, for up to 5s",
          "nodes": [
            {
              "label": "check the page",
              "sub": "is it true yet?",
              "color": "blue",
              "atWord": 1.833
            },
            {
              "label": "not true yet",
              "sub": "no verdict written",
              "color": "orange",
              "atWord": 3.417
            },
            {
              "label": "wait a moment",
              "sub": "then check again",
              "color": "purple",
              "atWord": 5.917
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "durationFrames": 385,
      "audio": "audio/pw-dojo-06-assertions_long_s12.mp3",
      "timingSource": "tts"
    },
    {
      "id": "s13",
      "type": "CODE_DIFF",
      "transition": "push",
      "background": "zoneA",
      "narration": "So in your tests, one line goes out and one line comes in. And when something is genuinely slow, like a report that takes ten seconds to build, you hand the critic more patience instead of reaching for sleep.",
      "data": {
        "diff": {
          "fileName": "test_save.py",
          "stat": {
            "plus": 4,
            "minus": 1
          },
          "atWord": 9.5,
          "rows": [
            {
              "kind": "ctx",
              "text": "# BAD — checks once, at the worst possible moment:"
            },
            {
              "kind": "del",
              "text": "assert page.get_by_text(\"Success\").is_visible()"
            },
            {
              "kind": "ctx",
              "text": ""
            },
            {
              "kind": "ctx",
              "text": "# GOOD — retries for up to 5s until true:"
            },
            {
              "kind": "add",
              "text": "expect(page.get_by_text(\"Success\")).to_be_visible()"
            },
            {
              "kind": "ctx",
              "text": ""
            },
            {
              "kind": "ctx",
              "text": "# custom patience for slow things:"
            },
            {
              "kind": "add",
              "text": "expect("
            },
            {
              "kind": "add",
              "text": "    page.get_by_text(\"Report ready\")"
            },
            {
              "kind": "add",
              "text": ").to_be_visible(timeout=15000)"
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "durationFrames": 383,
      "audio": "audio/pw-dojo-06-assertions_long_s13.mp3",
      "timingSource": "tts"
    },
    {
      "id": "s14",
      "type": "REVEAL",
      "transition": "iris",
      "background": "zoneB",
      "narration": "Is a plain assert ever right? Yes. For a value you have already pulled out of the page and hold in a variable, there is nothing left to wait for. A number you computed will not change while you look at it.",
      "data": {
        "reveal": {
          "kicker": "the exception",
          "statement": "assert is fine for values, not for the page",
          "sub": "nothing on a live page is ever settled",
          "atWord": 2.5
        }
      },
      "durationFrames": 351,
      "audio": "audio/pw-dojo-06-assertions_long_s14.mp3",
      "timingSource": "tts"
    },
    {
      "id": "s15",
      "type": "QUIZ_CARD",
      "transition": "push",
      "background": "zoneA",
      "narration": "First check. A success toast appears about one second after you click Save. Which check is reliable? Have a think, and pause the video if you want longer. Ready? It is C. Expect keeps re-checking until that toast turns up.",
      "data": {
        "quiz": {
          "question": "A toast appears 1s after Save. Which check is reliable?",
          "options": [
            {
              "text": "assert loc.is_visible()"
            },
            {
              "text": "time.sleep(3), then assert"
            },
            {
              "text": "expect(loc).to_be_visible()"
            },
            {
              "text": "No check needed"
            }
          ],
          "answerIndex": 2,
          "why": "expect() re-checks until the toast appears. sleep wastes 3s every run.",
          "revealAtWord": 25.417,
          "atWord": 4.5
        }
      },
      "durationFrames": 440,
      "audio": "audio/pw-dojo-06-assertions_long_s15.mp3",
      "timingSource": "tts"
    },
